(text "TREMOR-CANCELING SMART SPOON - electronics FINAL REV 2.0 (2026-10-24)" (at 20 256.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid d5226c6c-fbf0-5557-8c39-e8312252d3d2))
(text "Connections are made by NET LABELS: every pin with the same label is wired together. Wire list: wiring_table.csv" (at 20 259.20 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 7e15279b-e94a-5032-aebb-69adb88a69a9))
(text "Wire every module by its SILKSCREEN pin names (SimpleFOC Mini v1.0 / v1.1 header order differs)." (at 20 262.40 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6e704239-9a9e-5668-8a89-c1f520433b76))
(text "1) TPS61088: only the 12V pad bridged. Measure 12.0 V, and 5.0 V after the Mini560, BEFORE connecting anything else." (at 20 265.60 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid cfebd42a-e3ad-5696-9f22-f0f880f61991))
(text "2) System ground is the TP4056 OUT- pad, never B-. Charge through the TP4056 USB-C with SW1 OFF." (at 20 268.80 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 461d4757-3b94-5a75-9f13-f32df351219f))
(text "3) Both AS5600 have address 0x36 -> one per I2C bus. Bridge AS5600 chip pins 1-2 for 3.3 V. DIR to GND." (at 20 272.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid c86b9635-0be2-50c1-8218-791d7a7cb1d2))
(text "4) MOTOR_EN has a 100k pull-down: both drivers stay off until the firmware runs." (at 20 275.20 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid ab8b2bb1-09d7-55a9-b338-03b67420b75a))
(text "5) ESP32-S3 GPIOs are 3.3 V only. All pull-ups go to +3V3 (never 5 V or 12 V)." (at 20 278.40 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3252cf9a-dec6-5948-8544-0754bc0743e0))
(text "Firmware pin map: 04_firmware/TremorSpoon/src/config.h  (cross-checked by check_design.py)." (at 20 281.60 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 951344b0-b37a-536b-af97-f4871a556fd4))
